# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  PASTE YOUR MONGODB CONNECTION STRING ON LINE 5, THEN SAVE.
#  That is the ONLY thing required. Everything else is optional.
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
MONGODB_URI=


# ── GOOGLE SIGN-IN (optional) ─── paste on lines 9 and 10 ──────
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=


# ── ADMIN PASSKEY ── opens the dashboard. Change if you like.
ADMIN_PASSKEY=2010J


# ── IMAGE HOSTING (optional) ─── paste on lines 18, 19, 20 ─────
CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME=
CLOUDINARY_API_KEY=
CLOUDINARY_API_SECRET=


# ── GOOGLE MAPS (optional) ────── paste on line 24 ─────────────
NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=


# ── EMAIL (optional) ──────────── paste on line 28 ─────────────
RESEND_API_KEY=
EMAIL_FROM=BPSF <noreply@buypersqft.com>


# ── APP URL ── change only when you deploy to a real domain
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=http://localhost:3000


# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  NOTES — you do not need to read these to get started
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
#  MONGODB_URI  (line 5)
#    https://cloud.mongodb.com → create a free cluster →
#    "Connect" → "Drivers" → copy the string → replace <password>
#    with your database user's password.
#    Under "Network Access" add 0.0.0.0/0 while developing.
#
#    It looks like:
#    mongodb+srv://user:pass@cluster0.abcde.mongodb.net/bpsf?retryWrites=true&w=majority
#
#  GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID / SECRET  (lines 9, 10)
#    https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials
#      1. Create or pick a project
#      2. "OAuth consent screen" → External → app name + your email → Save
#      3. "Credentials" → "+ CREATE CREDENTIALS" → "OAuth client ID"
#      4. Application type: "Web application"
#      5. Under "Authorised redirect URIs" → ADD URI → paste EXACTLY:
#              http://localhost:3000/api/auth/google/callback
#         (character-for-character, or Google returns redirect_uri_mismatch)
#      6. Create → copy the Client ID and Client secret into lines 9 and 10
#    Leave blank and the site still works — the Google button just says
#    sign-in isn't configured. Email/password sign-in is unaffected.
#
#  CLOUDINARY  (lines 18-20)
#    https://cloudinary.com/console — all three values are on the dashboard.
#    Leave blank and property images save to public/uploads/ on this machine.
#    That is fine locally; on a cloud host those files are wiped on redeploy.
#
#  NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY  (line 24)
#    Same Google console → "+ CREATE CREDENTIALS" → "API key",
#    then enable "Maps JavaScript API" under APIs & Services → Library.
#    Restrict it by HTTP referrer — this one is used in the browser.
#
#  RESEND_API_KEY  (line 28)
#    https://resend.com/api-keys
#    Leave blank and emails print to the terminal instead of sending.
#
#  SESSION SECRETS — handled automatically
#    Signing keys are derived from MONGODB_URI, so there is nothing to
#    generate. If you prefer explicit keys in production, add:
#        JWT_ACCESS_SECRET=<64+ random chars>
#        JWT_REFRESH_SECRET=<a different 64+ random chars>
#    Setting them invalidates existing sessions once, then stays stable.
